  "zipball_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/DocumentDrivenDX/truss/zipball/v0.0.48",
  "body": "\n# Truss v0.0.48\n\n## Release scope\n\nCandidate for Python embedders and operators; publication remains gated by the\n[follow-up plan](../hohfeld-followup-plan-20261021.md). Python3.11+, PostgreSQL18.6,\npsycopg3.3.6, mini-racer0.14.1, UMF0.10 and Weft0.4.51 form the selected tuple.\nNative0.74-candidate has manifest SHA-256\n`c4339ac7f09ab5a004c272ab00962107a970938004c1765ec4163e4d5ca9b6f0`.\nRelease assets and this guide communicate the changes to embedders/operators.\n\n## Highlights and changes\n\n- Finite person entrypoints return typed nonmembership refusals while actual\n  damaged EXECUTE grants remain native execution errors. Statement-stable data\n  sources retain their original snapshot with independently current authorization.\n- Frozen complete group requests support observer-only recovery. Missing,\n  conflicting or unauthorized observations never execute the group again.\n- Empty Records allow the paired core/DDD required-field addition; populated\n  Records refuse it, including retained matching values. Existing qualified\n  core-only retained-value rebinds continue to work.\n- Weft-owned descriptors, explicit ordered entity facts and relationship\n  projections, typed resolver diagnostics, selected indexed predicates and key\n  pages use query ABI1.2. Other domains retain bounded complete fallback reads.\n- Completion and group dry-run force only Truss's deferred constraints and\n  publish observation carriers after host-owned rollback. They preserve prior\n  caller work and produce no durable receipt or committed created identity.\n- Authorized cross-module audit discovery, whole mutation metadata up to4,096\n  events within its byte bound, and optional reader-authorized archived key/version\n  projections. Relationship-only load discovery/details now retain exact owners\n  and actor names; old incomplete headers remain unavailable.\n- Deduplicated import owner inventories reduce measured residual import work;\n  all original inputs still receive authorization checks. Performance evidence\n  is workload-specific and establishes no general latency/p95 target.\n- Original `arras.view` version0.1.0 Record/Field metadata is preserved through queries\n  under its exact owning-document declaration; unsupported selected declarations\n  refuse. Unknown unselected content and source bytes/pins remain intact.\n- The independent corpus archive and installed runner are release assets.\n\n## Required actions and migration\n\nOnly the latest runtime is supported. Admitted previous databases migrate\nforward without a release-age cutoff. Previous application releases do not\nremain supported. This release retains the original0.0.44, shared0.0.45/46 and\n0.0.47 migration sources and all immutable prior recipe/receipt evidence.\n\nQuiesce writers and back up both database and host recovery registry. Follow\n[the migration guide](../../../../packages/python/README.md#runtime-migrations--v0048):\ninspect status, prepare and retain the reference, apply that reference, reconcile\nuncertain settlement, and verify before resuming latest application work.\nStartup never migrates. One complete route publishes one final receipt; prior\nreceipts remain unchanged. Install the matching Weft0.4.51 query dependency.\n\nExact text ACL inventories now distinguish sibling overloads. Separately pinned\nsupplements strengthen old-profile admission without rewriting published source\nprofiles. Native drift refuses before effects. Logical restores require the\noriginal backup-metadata companion for PostgreSQL's omitted row-type ACLs.\n\n## Hold and recovery\n\nHold on drift, failed verification or uncertain settlement. Reconcile the same\noriginal attempt; do not repeat effects with a new request. Pre-commit failure\nrolls back; committed changes require a forward fix or the qualified backup\nrestore/remigration workflow. Installing an old package is not database rollback.\n\n## Qualification and known limits\n\nLocal macOS ARM64 and hosted Linux x86_64 qualification are separate gates.\nThe [source-F local candidate](../evidence/hohfeld-followup-20261021/installed-048-arras-source557/receipt.json)\npasses 80 migration cases, 62 independent corpus cases and six compiler-cohort\ncontrols without skips. The enabled policy suite passes 14 executions covering\n10 distinct controls (four imported query tests repeat), and the original\n1,000-object/1,000-edge workload passes. The actual compiler/build source is\n`557153731e9f5d0583193a1189a07c6ed485d3d3`; all 455 runtime payloads match the\nsource, wheel and sdist. Earlier skipped/failed attempts remain preserved with\ntheir original outcomes, including one policy activation statement timeout and\nthe successful same-limit serialized retry. The independent archive's reviewed\nsingle producer-pin amendment preserves the original source, corpus and refusal\nlog; no test assertion changed.\n\nThe conformance runner and publication gate verify exact compiler module/source\nidentity beyond its version string. Public Weft adoption, final Truss Linux tag\nqualification and fresh public-artifact receipts remain mandatory. No publication\nis claimed by this draft.\n\nNo pre-0.10 or protected-profile migration, downgrade, managed-service support,\nother driver qualification or perpetual old runtime execution is added. Unknown\nextension content remains preserved. Ordinary receipts remain indefinitely\nretained; expiry observer fixtures do not establish an expiry writer. Broader\nquery domains and p95 targets remain outside the selected evidence.\n"
